  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Skills Development Programme and Policy and Labour Market Governance for Improved Employability of Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This output focuses on strengthening national employment services and labour market programmes to better support people in their transitions to decent work. It promotes inclusive and responsive systems that address the specific needs of women, youth and older persons, and that are equipped to respond effectively to changing labour market dynamics and crisis situations, including in the rural areas.

Support is also provided to the Government to formulate, implement and evaluate inclusive employment-intensive public investment programmes both in urban and rural areas. These programmes aim to generate more and better jobs, improve livelihoods and contribute to sustainable and resilient recovery, particularly in contexts affected by economic shocks, climate-related events or other crises.</narrative>
  </description>
